oride</source><year>2005</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>307</fpage><lpage>311</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b8-ijerph-06-00710"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Karro</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Indermitte</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Saava</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Haamer</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Marandi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fluoride occurrence in publicly supplied drinking water in Estonia</article-title><source>Environ. Geol</source><year>2006</year><volume>50</volume><fpage>389</fpage><lpage>396</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b9-ijerph-06-00710"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kiik</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><source>Joogivee erineva fluorisisalduse m&#x000f5;just laste hammaskonna seisundile Eesti NSV tingimustes. [The influence of different fluoride content in drinking water to dental status of children in Estonian SSR]</source>Doctoral thesis; <publisher-name>Research Institute of Epidemiology, Microbiology and Hygiene</publisher-name> <publisher-loc>Tallinn, Estonia</publisher-loc><year>1970</year>(in Estonian).</citation></ref><ref id="b10-ijerph-06-00710"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Indermitte</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Russak</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Saava</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The contribution of drinking water towards dental fluorosis: A case study in Tartu</article-title><source>Paper Anthropol</source><year>2005</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>97</fpage><lpage>109</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b11-ijerph-06-00710"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Indermitte</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Karro</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Saava</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tap water fluoride levels in Estonia</article-title><source>Fluoride</source><year>2007</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>227</fpage><lpage>230</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b12-ijerph-06-00710"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dean</surname><given-names>HT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Classification of mottled enamel diagnosis</article-title><source>J. Am. Dent. Assoc</source><year>1934</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>1421</fpage><lpage>1426</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b13-ijerph-06-00710"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>WHO</collab><source>Oral Health Surveys Basic Methods</source><edition>4th</edition><publisher-name>World Health Organisation</publisher-name><publisher-loc>Geneva, Switzerland</publisher-loc><year>1997</year></citation></ref><ref id="b14-ijerph-06-00710"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cameron</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Widmer</surname><given-names>RP</given-names></name></person-group><source>Handbook of pediatric dentistry</source><publisher-name>Mosby</publisher-name><publisher-loc>London, UK</publisher-loc><year>1997</year></citation></ref><ref id="b15-ijerph-06-00710"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zohouri</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Rugg-Gunn</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sources of dietary fluoride intake in 4-year-old children